  "problem": "| $x$ | $1$ | $4$ | $6$ | $8$ |\n| --- | --- | --- | --- | --- |\n| $f(x)$ | $0.4$ | $0.25$ | $0.1$ | $0.25$ |\n\nLet ${X}_{1},{X}_{2},…,{X}_{128}$ be a random sample of size $n=128$ from a population with the probability mass function given above.  Find an approximation for the probability that the sample mean is between $3.6$ and $4.2.$\n\n*Hint: Two tables of values of $Φ(z)$ for different values of $z$ are given below, where $Φ(z)$ is the cumulative distribution function for the standard normal distribution. *\n\n<table align=\"center\">\n\n<tbody><tr>\n<th>\n<table align=\"center\" cellpadding=\"5\" rules=\"all\">\n<tbody><tr> \n  <th width=\"25%\" bgcolor=\"#D6EAF8\" align=\"center\">$z$</th>\n  <th bgcolor=\"#D6EAF8\" align=\"center\">$\\,0.00\\,$</th>\n  <th bgcolor=\"#D6EAF8\" align=\"center\">$\\,0.01\\,$</th>\n  <th bgcolor=\"#D6EAF8\" align=\"center\">$\\,0.02\\,$</th>\n</tr>\n<tr> \n  <th bgcolor=\"#D6EAF8\" align=\"center\">$\\,0.7\\,$</th>\n  <td align=\"center\"> $\\,0.7580\\,$ </td>\n  <td align=\"center\"> $\\,0.7611\\,$ </td>\n  <td align=\"center\"> $\\,0.7642\\,$ </td>\n</tr>\n<tr> \n  <th bgcolor=\"#D6EAF8\" align=\"center\">$\\,0.8\\,$</th>\n    <td align=\"center\"> $\\,0.7881\\,$ </td>\n    <td align=\"center\"> $\\,0.7910\\,$ </td>\n    <td align=\"center\"> $\\,0.7939\\,$ </td>\n</tr>\n<tr> \n  <th bgcolor=\"#D6EAF8\" align=\"center\">$\\,0.9\\,$</th>\n  <td align=\"center\"> $\\,0.8159\\,$ </td>\n  <td align=\"center\"> $\\,0.8186\\,$ </td>\n  <td align=\"center\"> $\\,0.8212\\,$ </td>\n</tr>\n</tbody></table>\n\n<p></p></th>\n<th width=\"5%\"></th>\n\n<th><p></p>\n<table align=\"center\" cellpadding=\"5\" rules=\"all\">\n<tbody><tr> \n  <th width=\"25%\" bgcolor=\"#D6EAF8\" align=\"center\">$z$</th>\n  <th bgcolor=\"#D6EAF8\" align=\"center\">$\\,0.00\\,$</th>\n  <th bgcolor=\"#D6EAF8\" align=\"center\">$\\,0.01\\,$</th>\n  <th bgcolor=\"#D6EAF8\" align=\"center\">$\\,0.02\\,$</th>\n</tr>\n<tr> \n  <th bgcolor=\"#D6EAF8\" a